text:
alex: Heads-up — spotted a problematic retry pattern in the onboarding sample apps. The Go sample treats all 4xx as transient and retries, which triggers token refresh storms. Repro: sampleapp/go/client.go uses isTransient(resp.StatusCode) for retries.

mira: Oof. Can you paste the exact snippet? is it in sdk helper or the wrapper?

alex: It's in the sample wrapper around SendWithRetry. Minimal code:```go
resp, err := client.Do(req)
if isTransient(resp.StatusCode) {
  return RetryWithBackoff()
}
```
Server returned `403 Forbidden` with body `{"error":"forbidden: api key lacks scope"}` and the sample keeps retrying / refreshing tokens.

dylan: That explains a bunch. Our intended mapping is 401 -> AuthError (refresh token once), 403 -> PermissionDenied (do not refresh). Looks like Go SDK parity bug: isTransient treats 4xx as retryable. Python is correct.
sam: This matches incoming support tickets where customers see spikes in token-refresh and then get ratelimited. We should patch the Go SDK logic and update the sample README to show the correct pattern. Also change README wording from "catch errors and retry" to explicit guidance. :facepalm:

alex: Suggested onboarding snippet for clarity:```pseudo
if IsAuthError(err) {
  refreshToken();
  retryOnce();
} else if IsRetryable(err) {
  retryWithBackoff();
} else {
  surfaceErrorToUser();
}
```
Add a comment explaining 403 is non-retryable because it's a permission/scopes issue.

mira: I'll open a docs PR to patch the READMEs for both python and go samples. Will include an explanation & code examples showing auth vs permission vs transient errors.

dylan: I'll own the SDK fix. Plan: change Go MapHTTPStatusToError so 401 -> AuthError(retry_hint: "refresh"), 403 -> PermissionError(retry_hint: "none"). Add unit tests for 401/403/429 and an integration test simulating stale token + forbidden. Branch `fix/go-4xx-map` and PR by EOD.

ci-bot: CI: go-tests-retry-matrix failing — 4 tests in `retry_matrix_test.go`. See https://ci.example.com/builds/4832

qa-bot: Created ticket RW-3421: "Go SDK: correct 4xx mapping; update onboarding sample app." Assigned to dylan. Test matrix includes 401, 403, 429 and idempotency scenarios.

sam: For long-term ergonomics, propose standard error shape across SDKs: fields: `code` (string), `message` (string), `http_status` (int/string), `retry_hint` (enum: none|backoff|refresh|idempotent), `recovery_hint` (human string). This avoids sticky string matching in apps.

alex: Strong +1. Also update sample README to recommend sending Idempotency-Key for POSTs and only auto-retrying on idempotent retry_hint or 5xx/429. Example header:```http
POST /v1/complete
Idempotency-Key: 123e4567
```

mira: I'll add those examples and a short onboarding note: "Do not auto-refresh on 403; check retry_hint and status." Will also add a tiny checklist for SDK maintainers to keep parity.

dylan: I'll bump the Go SDK minor version and add CHANGELOG note that 4xx mapping behavior is tightened (should be low risk but may change retry behavior for some apps).

ci-bot: After PR merge, CI will run `retry-matrix` and `sample-app-smoke`. Docs PR should reference specific sample commit so onboarding docs can point to the fixed sample.

sam: Great. Once merged let's monitor support queues for a week to confirm token-refresh storms drop. Thanks everyone. :thumbsup:
